# What the second round of review found.

[break] worktree-include-negation-under-an-ignored-folder
rule: A `!` line cannot take back a file under an ignored folder: git does not look inside one.
file: xtask/src/rules/worktree_include.rs
in: ignored
find: (1..parts.len()).any(|length| verdict(&parts[..length], true, patterns))
replace: false
caught-by:
    rules::worktree_include::tests::a_file_under_an_ignored_folder_stays_ignored

[break] pty-keys-an-index-read-as-bytes
rule: Only an array literal (after `&`, `(`, `,` or `[`) holds bytes: a `[` after a name or a bracket is an index.
file: xtask/src/rules/pty_keys.rs
in: keys_of_arguments
find: .is_some_and(|before| matches!(text(before), "&" | "(" | "," | "["))
replace: .is_some()
caught-by:
    rules::pty_keys::tests::a_number_that_is_not_an_array_of_bytes_passes

[break] pty-keys-a-repeat-read-as-bytes
rule: A repeat (`[b'x'; 27]`) is no array of the bytes in it.
file: xtask/src/rules/pty_keys.rs
in: keys_of_arguments
find: *frame = None;
replace: let _ = frame;
caught-by:
    rules::pty_keys::tests::a_number_that_is_not_an_array_of_bytes_passes

[break] pty-keys-local-helper-not-a-sender
rule: A function of the file whose body calls `.send(` is a sender: its literal arguments are read.
file: xtask/src/rules/pty_keys.rs
